                <pb facs="1082" n="1074" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg1074"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6731/412a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-27T18:00:00-04:00">July 27, 1938—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18. The Turkish Ambassador called at the Department on July 25 under instructions
                    from his Government to submit a copy of the Turkish Government’s latest
                        proposal<anchor n="26" xml:id="d876-f1"/> with respect to the general
                    provisions in the proposed trade agreement relating to binding of duty
                    reductions, exchange control, and duration of agreement. If the Delegation has
                    not yet received a copy of this proposal, you should request one from the
                    Turkish authorities at the earliest opportunity, and telegraph the Department
                    (1) your comments and recommendations with reference thereto and (2) the
                    reasons, if known, for this action on the part of the Turkish Government in
                    transmitting its proposal through the Ambassador here rather than through the
                    Delegation at Ankara.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
